'20261121_1603_M7_round3_relationship_audit.sql','2026-11-21T16:03:57+08:00','Win-M7','M7','role/M7-audit','DeepSeek Harness',
'AI drove the Access COM automation, wrote the datasheet and DAO/SQL test harnesses, generated the markdown audit report, and drafted this log entry. The auditor reviewed every captured message against the blueprint text and ran the independence check before reading the M6 log.',
'Round 3 blind test of all 46 fields plus the PK, FK and 12-relationship audit on an independent copy of the M3 release database.',
'Round 3 must be independent and must not copy R1/R2 results, so the whole 46-field matrix was re-driven from the workbook rather than re-used. Datasheet automation proved unreliable for commit-time validation on this machine, so each R3 stimulus was applied a second time as a single DAO/SQL UPDATE and the message text was captured verbatim from the engine; rows carry the track that produced their evidence, so no unobserved UI dialog is claimed. The 46 fields match the blueprint exactly, therefore no schema change is requested.',
'workspaces/R7_Forms/Round3_Audit_Log.md (189 lines); workspaces/R7_Forms/Round3_And_Relationship_Audit.md (identical copy under the SOP P0 name); input db workspaces/R7_Forms/Inputs/v1_Core_Seeded.accdb SHA256 5779B94439854514F6B32F3BADBF8B132ABF8FD22CAC35AECF3D000D14974127 (same hash as the M3 handoff); workbook workspaces/R7_Forms/Inputs/Sample_Data_Master_M7.xlsx SHA256 A356A9C4F415682E606AEE2D0BF0C4D598697965FF97019F1791B908246528ED; source commit 810b6031c3f4eef8cb815ee51d8e2cd3ee2adb13; Access 16.0.20527.20196; relation screenshot _m7work/p34_relations.png and _m7work/p36_relations_all.png (local, not committed).',
'Assumed the workbook column R3 M7 input defines the R3 stimulus for each field, and that FieldSize+1 characters is the intended size test. Four extra checks were run outside the 46 rows (reverse interaction pair, self-link interaction, future BirthDate, future ReceiptDate) and are reported separately as supplementary.',
'workspaces/R7_Forms/Round3_Audit_Log.md; workspaces/R7_Forms/Round3_And_Relationship_Audit.md; handoff_logs/entries/20261121_1603_M7_round3_relationship_audit.sql',
'PASS',
'46 of 46 workbook rows executed and matched their expected outcome. PK: 7 AutoNumber single keys plus the 3 junction tables that really carry two-column primary keys. FK: all 12 foreign keys are Long Integer and Required. Relationships: 12 relations, every one with Attributes 0 (referential integrity enforced, cascade delete and cascade update both off), every parent on the 1 side, and parent deletes for all 7 populated parent tables refused, which proves no cascade delete path exists. Verbatim rule texts match the blueprint word for word. Afterwards the test copy was restored to the baseline SHA256, so no test data remains. LIMITATION: under automation the datasheet frequently did not reach the commit point, so field-level validation dialogs were captured only for the required-field case, tblMedication.ListPrice and the Zoom overlength box; every other rule, required and datatype row is evidenced by the engine track and is labelled as such. Two datasheet tracks also exist, so R3 is not a pure click-through test.',
'None for the database. Open only for method reporting: the dashboard of visible datasheet dialogs is thinner than in R1/R2 because of the automation limit above.',
'M3 and M8 can consume the report as is. Do not edit the message texts to match R1/R2, and do not restate engine rows as datasheet observations. If a marking demo needs every dialog on screen, re-run the rule rows by hand and append the observed text, keeping the existing rows intact.'
);
